{"path":"string/basic_string/clear","title":"std::basic_string<CharT,Traits,Allocator>::clear","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::basic_string&lt;CharT,Traits,Allocator&gt;::</span>clear","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string/clear","section":"string","kind":"page","summary":"Removes all characters from the string as if by executing erase(begin(), end()).","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td><div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span> clear<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> </td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(noexcept since C++11)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(constexpr since C++20)</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Removes all characters from the string as if by executing <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">erase<span class=\"br0\">(</span>begin<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, end<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</p><p>All pointers, references, and iterators are invalidated.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Unlike for <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/vector/clear\">std::vector::clear</a></span>, the C++ standard does not explicitly require that <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string/capacity\">capacity</a></span> is unchanged by this function, but existing implementations do not change capacity. This means that they do not release the allocated memory (see also <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string/shrink_to_fit\">shrink_to_fit</a></span>).\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Complexity\">Complexity</h3>\n<p>Linear in the size of the string, although existing implementations operate in constant time.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cassert&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;string&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1238\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a> s<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"st0\">\"Exemplar\"</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">string</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">size_type</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> capacity <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> s.<span class=\"me1\">capacity</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    s.<span class=\"me1\">clear</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/assert\"><span class=\"kw778\">assert</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>s.<span class=\"me1\">empty</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/assert\"><span class=\"kw778\">assert</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>s.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/manip/boolalpha\"><span class=\"kw1781\">std::<span class=\"me2\">boolalpha</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>s.<span class=\"me1\">capacity</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> capacity<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>true</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string/erase\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>erase</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  removes characters <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Complexity","id":"Complexity"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"string","title":"Strings library"},{"path":"string/basic_string","title":"std::basic_string"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::basic_string<CharT,Traits,Allocator>::clear","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Removes all characters from the string as if by executing erase(begin(), end())."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Return value","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Notes","note":"Unlike for std::vector::clear, the C++ standard does not explicitly require that capacity is unchanged by this function, but existing implementations do not…"},{"label":"Complexity","note":"Linear in the size of the string, although existing implementations operate in constant time."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"erase","note":"removes